    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside trio in the outfield. **Mickey Moniak** leads the way with an elite 75.75 efficiency score, bolstered by a massive +14% park factor and a significant platoon edge that makes him our primary target against Freddy Peralta. Joining him, **James Wood** (73.62) provides a high-floor spark at the top of the order; his elite 0.377 xwOBA and favorable matchup against Ober create excellent run-scoring potential. Meanwhile, **Brice Turang** (66.93) remains a vital asset for our stolen base-starved roster, as his matchup against Pallante\u2014combined with a +4% boost for facing a pitcher with a slow delivery\u2014positions him to capitalize on his elite sprint speed today.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Austin Riley**, who scored a 48.84 but ultimately fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace our current starters. While **Austin Riley** offers perennial power, his unfavorable matchup against Woo and a negative park factor forced our hand toward the higher-ceiling platoon advantages presented by players like **Trevor Story** and **Seiya Suzuki**. We are exercising caution with **Gabriel Moreno** and **Tyler Soderstrom**; both face elite arms in Skenes and Wheeler, respectively, and while their inclusion helps preserve our game caps, their low scores reflect the significant risk of tangling with such high-caliber pitching. We are also monitoring **Jose Caballero** on the bench; despite his potential for speed, the combination of a daunting matchup against Eovaldi, a bottom-of-the-order projection, and a 44% rain risk necessitated keeping him sidelined for this slate.",
